<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ubi caritas, Quatre Motets sur des thèmes grégoriens No. 1 (Maurice Duruflé)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">choral setting on the Gregorian melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Where Charity and Love Prevail</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English translation (copyrighted)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ubi caritas (Jacques Berthier, Taizé)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chant on the refrain</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ubi caritas (Paul Halley)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the chant combined with other songs on Angel on a Stone Wall</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ubi caritas (Ola Gjeilo)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">choral setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ubi caritas (Paul Mealor)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2011</span><span class="sg-chain-h">choral setting, sung at a royal wedding</span></li></ul></section>
